  "ai_show_review": {
    "summary": "High‑energy Alpine Valley ’82 with smoking Let It Grow, Wheel & China>Rider",
    "review": "The August 7 1982 Alpine Valley show is a pure burst of late‑summer fire. From the opening “Music Never Stopped” > Sugaree > “Music Never Stopped” sandwich to an inspired second set, the band rides a relentless groove. Jerry’s voice is described as \"on, on, on\" and his guitar rockets into another dimension during Let It Grow, while Brent’s keyboards add that space‑y sparkle behind Playin’ > Wheel. The highlight reel includes a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, an incendiary Wheel, and a soaring Morning Dew that lands perfectly into One More Saturday Night.  Across the board the energy stays high, the segues lock in tight, and the rhythm section—Phil’s bass (even when a little muddy on audience tapes), Bill & Mickey’s pounding drums, and Brent’s vocal‑harmonized keys—drives the whole thing forward.\n\nIn terms of listening experience the crisp, crystalline soundboard captured by the Streeter‑Wise tape (gd82-08-07.sbd‑streeter‑wise.unknown.7689.sbeok.shnf) is the gold standard: excellent board quality with no drop‑outs and a balanced mix that lets every instrument breathe. While the Serafin SBD is solid, it suffers from the typical thin mids of ’82 boards; the Streeter‑Wise version delivers the clarity needed to truly appreciate the fire in Jerry’s leads and the tightness of the rhythm section. Whether you’re after the sheer power of the Wheel or the delicate beauty of Let It Grow, this recording lets you hear every nuance of one of the band’s high points on the Alpine Valley stage.",
